1
00:00:00,185 --> 00:00:01,990
Sailors feared the monster Scylla.

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:03,200
None knew who made her:

3
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:05,689
a lonely girl with a basket of flowers.

4
00:00:05,931 --> 00:00:07,240
The Greek gods ruled the world,

5
00:00:07,240 --> 00:00:09,525
and played with mortals like toys.

6
00:00:09,525 --> 00:00:10,440
Yellow flowers grew

7
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:12,330
where Titan blood had soaked the earth.

8
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:13,420
Their sap could change

9
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:15,150
a creature into its truest self.

10
00:00:15,150 --> 00:00:16,840
Circe, daughter of the sun god,

11
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:18,643
was mocked by her own family.

12
00:00:18,643 --> 00:00:19,920
Then she met Glaucos,

13
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:21,758
a poor fisherman who was kind to her.

14
00:00:21,758 --> 00:00:23,440
To keep him, she fed him the sap.

15
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:24,728
He became a sea god.

16
00:00:24,728 --> 00:00:26,640
A god had no use for Circe.

17
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:28,560
He chose Scylla, a beautiful nymph,

18
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:30,120
who flaunted his gifts.

19
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:31,200
That night, Circe poured

20
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:32,880
the sap into Scylla's bathing pool,

21
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:34,460
to show the world how ugly

22
00:00:34,460 --> 00:00:35,640
she was inside.

23
00:00:35,879 --> 00:00:36,730
Scylla screamed.

24
00:00:37,180 --> 00:00:38,560
Six necks burst from the water,

25
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:40,205
six mouths, forever hungry.

26
00:00:40,437 --> 00:00:41,780
From a cliff above the sea,

27
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:43,869
she snatched sailors from passing ships.

28
00:00:43,869 --> 00:00:45,510
The gods exiled Circe.

29
00:00:45,760 --> 00:00:46,880
Years later, she learned how

30
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,328
many men Scylla had eaten.

31
00:00:48,328 --> 00:00:50,086
Every one of them was her fault.

32
00:00:50,086 --> 00:00:51,680
Centuries later, she went back

33
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:53,153
to face what she made.

34
00:00:53,153 --> 00:00:54,100
She couldn't undo it.

35
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:55,800
So she turned Scylla to stone,

36
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:57,041
the only peace left.

37
00:00:57,475 --> 00:00:59,230
Scylla never chose to be a monster.

38
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:00,302
Circe did.

39
00:01:00,545 --> 00:01:01,160
She wanted the world

40
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:02,650
to see Scylla's true face.

41
00:01:02,860 --> 00:01:05,226
In the end, the flowers showed her own.
